# Line endings.
#
# Everyone on this team is on Windows, where Git's default is to convert files
# to CRLF on checkout. Prettier writes LF. Left alone, those two fight: Prettier
# rewrites a file to LF, Git converts it back to CRLF, and the next diff shows
# every line as changed when only one line really was.
#
# Forcing LF everywhere ends it. All modern tooling on Windows (VS Code, Node,
# Git Bash, Prettier) reads LF without complaint.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF. A CRLF line ending inside a script can stop it
# running at all — including .husky/pre-commit, which runs on every commit.
*.sh        text eol=lf
.husky/*    text eol=lf

# Binary files — Git must never rewrite these.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.docx      binary
